FINDINGS:

1. [MINOR] src/logging.rs:160 — An instant outside `chrono`'s representable range silently loses the timestamp field (`from_timestamp(secs, nanos)?` returns `None`), which is a third no-timestamp case beyond the two `SPEC.md` documents (timestamps turned off, and a host with no clock). The existing unit test at `src/logging.rs:318-323` pins this behaviour, so the code is intentional; the defect is that the documented record shape is incomplete for an out-of-range host clock. Fix: state the out-of-range case in `SPEC.md` alongside the no-clock case, or make the formatter return an error/clamped value instead of dropping the field. I could not run the tests; this is a docs/spec consistency finding, not a claim that the test is wrong.

2. [MINOR] src/logging.rs:222-223 — A captured `stdout` record is routed through `wasm::try_emit`, whose overflow branch at `src/wasm.rs:135-138` does `OVERFLOW.store(true); return Ok(())`. The logging call therefore reports success while the record is dropped, and the only failure is a later `Limit`; the SPEC promise that a destination that cannot be written is a catchable `IoError` naming `logging` does not hold for a full capture. Fix: give logging a fallible emit that returns `Err(WriteZero)` on overflow and map it to the same `IoError` naming `logging` (the run is still failed via `OVERFLOW`, so this is not an overall silent success).

REVIEW VERDICT: FINDINGS 2
